From: Josh Schmelzle <josh@joshschmelzle.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 11:48:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: WLAN Pi: deliver WMI mgmt RX to monitors when no monitor vdev runs

ath12k sets NO_VIRTUAL_MONITOR and marks every WMI management frame
RX_FLAG_SKIP_MONITOR, expecting the monitor vdev's ring to feed monitor
interfaces. That vdev only exists once a monitor vif holds a chanctx, so
a monitor created without a channel next to an AP or STA vif
(wlanpi-profiler's <if>profiler, wlanpi-core's wlanpiN) receives nothing
but our own TX. In hostapd mode the profiler never sees an association
request and never writes a profile.

Skip monitor delivery only while the monitor vdev is started. Otherwise
mac80211 copies the frame to monitors, as it does on virtual-monitor
drivers. The started-monitor path, and its duplicate avoidance, is
unchanged.

WLAN Pi local patch, not from ath-next.

Signed-off-by: Josh Schmelzle <josh@joshschmelzle.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c
index d5160af60..fbeb7f86e 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c
@@ -7385,8 +7385,11 @@ static void ath12k_mgmt_rx_event(struct ath12k_base *ab, struct sk_buff *skb)
 	/* Firmware is guaranteed to report all essential management frames via
 	 * WMI while it can deliver some extra via HTT. Since there can be
 	 * duplicates split the reporting wrt monitor/sniffing.
+	 * Without a started monitor vdev nothing feeds monitor interfaces,
+	 * so let mac80211 copy these frames to them.
 	 */
-	status->flag |= RX_FLAG_SKIP_MONITOR;
+	if (READ_ONCE(ar->monitor_started))
+		status->flag |= RX_FLAG_SKIP_MONITOR;
 
 	/* In case of PMF, FW delivers decrypted frames with Protected Bit set
 	 * including group privacy action frames.
